pages.content:
The **continue statement in a while loop** is used to skip the remaining code in the current iteration and move to the **next iteration** of the loop. It allows you to skip certain steps without breaking out of the loop entirely.

**Syntax:**
```c
while (condition) {
    // Loop body
    if (some_condition) {
        continue;  // Skips the remaining code in this iteration
    }
    // Code that will be skipped when the continue statement is executed
}
```
---
**Example:**
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int num = 18;

    while (num <= 25) {
        if (num % 2 == 0) {  // If the number is divisible by 2
            num++;            // Increment to check the next number
            continue;         // Skip printing numbers divisible by 2
        }

        printf("%d\n", num);  // Print the number if it's not divisible by 2
        num++;                // Increment to check the next number
    }

    return 0;
}
```
**Expected Output:**
```default
19
21
23
25
```

